I would go with weighted mean 1) logistic regression already gives higher weight to samples that are highly covered, this is just how it works, we don't change the default behaviour 2) imagine you have a region that is 50% methylated and covered 100X, if for some reason same region has less coverage in one sample such as 10X, you can simulate the situation by downsampling 100X region to 10X, if you do that you would get 20% or 80% methylated regions not infrequently.  So the moment you drop the coverage to 10X, you become less confident that your 10X covered CpG has the correct methylation level compared to same CpG covered 100X.

